@tradition new-hands-tea
// New hand's tea: your first Friday aboard (day 5). Works Friday tea, but for you: Calder hangs a mug with your name on
// the Works tea corner's rack, and it stays there all game. Same deck, same time as the weekly works-tea (18:45-19:30),
// and the rarer one wins, so that Friday it replaces it. New crew get their own on the Friday after they arrive
// (that needs a rotation rhythm: plans/trad-notes-seasons.md). The player is the honoree, so there's no {first}.
k: 480
title: New hand's tea
when: arrival friday
at: 18:40-19:30
min: 20
prio: 2
early: 5
where: 5 room Tea corner: lounge-seat
where: 5 room Works bay: work:works, free
where: 5 room Machine shop: work:works, free
where: 5 room Main storage: work:works, free
hold: 1
who: calder always, torres-zeke always, pell 95%, works 85%
anim: calder talk, everyone drink
host: calder
from: calder
ties: decor mugRack

== mail
- Friday tea tomorrow after dinner, {time}, Works tea corner. It's your first, so it's your new hand's tea. Bring nothing. That's the point.

== ask
- Friday tea tonight. Your first one. That's a big deal round here.
- New hand's tea after dinner. You don't have to make a speech.   #funny
- Don't be late tonight. There's a mug with your name on it.   #warm

== here
- Welcome to Works, properly.   #warm
- Your mug goes on the rack, next to mine. Don't let it get dusty.
- Everyone gets one on their first Friday. Mine has a chip in it.   #funny

== thanks
- Calder hangs a mug with your name on it on the rack and fills it. You're Works now.   #warm

== chatter
- The new hand's mug is up on the rack. It's a nice mug.
- I still remember my new hand's tea. I spilled mine on the Chief.   #funny
- Every name on that rack had a first Friday.   #warm
